{"reference":"Psalms 119","book":"Psalms","chapter":119,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Reading Psalm 119 in the Psalms","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"One way of locating Psalm 119 within the Psalms is to see it as part of Book V’s gathering of Torah meditation alongside return thanksgiving, festival praise, and Songs of Ascents oriented toward worship. This broader setting is debated, but it helps place the psalm’s sustained attention to God’s instruction within a collection that also preserves communal memories of destruction, exile, and return.","verse_refs":["Psalms 119:1-176"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_psalms_119_d1bc1e95ff621b9f7d75bb21"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}